AU  - Gilbert, P.
AU  - Zinaï, K.
PY  - 2024
PD  - 
N2  - Patient-centered care (PCC) was developed under pressure from public authorities, keen to preserve health systems whose financial balance is weakened by the aging of the population and the increase in chronic diseases. Renowned hospital institutions are promoting their patient-centered approach around the world. The Mayo Clinic in the United States is considered a pioneer of PCC in the world. In France, the implementation of PCC is not without raising questions, particularly in public hospitals. Some see it as an application of customer centricity from the commercial world. This chapter presents a study of PCC-labeled orthopedics department of a Parisian hospital. The study highlights different strategies for reconciling worlds, through compromises or arrangements, highlights the opportunity to adopt a project approach to avoid direct confrontation between worlds, and proposes solutions to implement PCC in public hospitals in an appeased manner. © ISTE Ltd 2024.
