N2  - So called Caisson's disease of bone is well recognized in the literature. The purpose of this paper is to move away from simply considering the orthopaedic aspects of avascular injury to bones and joints and provide some background physiology and physics to help understand the challenges encountered whilst diving. This is relevant to those working with professional divers. Either commercially or within the military setting, and some guidance will be provided for those involved in the acute care of divers injured or affected by the problems covered within this article. It is recommended that acute units that deal with diving accidents have established protocols to deal with the issues covered, including access to hyperbaric chambers. © 2022 Elsevier Ltd
