TI  - Berthold Epstein, Prague – the fate of a pediatrician between 1919 and 1962
AU  - Nolte, S.H.
PY  - 2023
PD  - 
N2  - The life of the pediatrician Berthold Epstein is representative for all the faults, which were unleashed by the First World War, culminating in millions of dead people in concentration camps, on battle fields and among civilians. The»othering«, the fear of the foreign, the racial hate, culminated in the desire for extermination by the National Socialists in order to eradicate the Jewish»race« once and for all. The name»Epstein« had wide renown during the great period of the evolving field of paediatrics before the First World War. Alois Epstein (1849–1918) had been the Director of the»Findelanstalt« in Prague since 1881 and had been Professor at the German Medical Faculty (DMF) since 1884. We owe him the naming»Epstein‘s pearls«, the gingival cysts in newborns, the naming»Epstein pseudodiphtheria« and particularly an orthopaedic furniture, the»Epstein-rockingchair«. Berthold Epstein was born on April 1st, 1890 in Pilsen. His father, Wilhelm Epstein (1853–1928), was Alois Epstein´s brother. The Jewish family came from Kamnitz an der Linde. Epstein was a»preventive arrest Jew« and was privileged compared with»transport Jews«, more importantly, he was a doctor. Josef Mengele summoned him to the»gypsy camp« B II e. Mengele intended to do research on a rare arisen disease, called Noma. In the»gypsy camp«, the disease broke out especially among children. For this, he recruited Epstein and wanted him to decide»voluntarily« to take over the position as a lead researcher. The involvement of Epstein in Mengele´s research activities other than that has not yet been fully solved. The children were accommodated in a relatively clean shack and received better food. Every time when Epstein´s team was successful in healing them, Mengele sent these children into the gas. Epstein stayed in Auschwitz until April 10th, 1945. Epstein was appointed by the Russian as leading doctor at the department of infectiology of the Red Army Hospital. When Epstein returned to Prague, almost his whole family was wiped out. After his return, he took up the work in his medical private practice, which he ran until 1957. Berthold Epstein died at an active stage of life on June 9th, 1962 at his place of work. © 2023 Mediengruppe Oberfranken - Fachverlage GmbH & Co. KG. All rights reserved.
