N2  - The story of orthodontics during the first 100 years of Journal publication can be told through the people who lived it. As part of the American Journal of Orthodontics and Dentofacial Orthopedics' Centennial celebration, we present 100 people who most influenced the specialty during the last 100 years. Part 2 picks up with "the greatest generation" and describes those born in the first 2 decades of the 20th century. Whether born in Europe or the United States, their lives and educations were disrupted by world war. Many served during the years of conflict, and a few paid an even heavier price. After World War II, they returned home or immigrated to the United States and resumed their life's work in orthodontics. © 2015 American Association of Orthodontists.
