TI  - Analysis on the composition of medical expense and drug use in the patients with clavicular fracture in 10 hospitals
AU  - Jiaming, B.
AU  - Yong, L.
AU  - Cang, C.
AU  - Jianhang, K.
AU  - Xu, H.
PY  - 2020
PD  - 
N2  - Objective:To study and evaluate the composition of medical expense and the rational drug use in treatment of the patients with clavicular fracture in 10 hospitals of different regions. Methods:The medical records that met the inclusion and exclusion criteria were retrieved from the database of the Military Monitoring Network for Rational Use of Drugs. The proportion of drug cost and material cost,drug amount and sum of money were summarized and analyzed. ResuHs:The average medical cost per patient was proportional to the cost level of the area where the hospital was located. There were significant differences in the average medical cost per patient,the proportion of drug cost and the drugs used to treat patients among different hospitals. Material cost was the heaviest economic burden for clavicular fracture patients treated with open internal fixation. The overall material cost accounted for 59. 7%,and was followed by drug cost (18. 7%). Orthopedics adjuvant drugs,neuro-adjuvant drugs and traditional Chinese medicine injections accounted for 35% of the total drug cost,and they constituted the main area of irrational drug use. Conclusion:The proportions of operation,anesthesia,treatment and nursing expense that reflected the value of medical staff were relatively low. There were significant differences in drug use in treatment of same diseases in different hospitals, indicating that the the problem of irrational drug use was quite prominent. The government should guide medical institutions to use drugs rationally and control the growth of medical expenses by further reforming the payment system of medical insurance and the salary system of medical personnel, so as to control the overgrowth of medical costs. © 2020 Publishing House of Pharmaceutical Care and Research. All rights reserved.
