N2  - The US military is in its longest wartime deployment in history. Military medical assets have been deployed in support of the nation’s military since the beginning of the conflicts in Afghanistan and Iraq and have achieved the highest survival rates in the history of US conflicts. Medical advances have improved the care of burn, blast, and penetrating trauma, as well as improved the return to function of wounded service members through advances in reconstructive surgery and rehabilitation. These lessons learned can be applied to the care of civilian casualties in war zones, natural disasters, and austere environments. © Springer International Publishing Switzerland 2016.
