TI  - Fracture care about the knee in high-energy war injuries
AU  - Andersen, R.C.
AU  - Pressman, D.N.
AU  - Keeling, J.J.
AU  - Gordon, W.
PY  - 2010
PD  - 
N2  - Current military conflicts in Iraq and Afghanistan have produced a new generation of high-energy musculoskeletal injuries, including those involving the knees. The bone and soft tissue contamination and destruction in these war injuries is often extensive and requires a systematic team approach from the initial point of injury on the overseas battle field to the definitive care treatment hospital. This article reviews the treatment methods used during the various echelons of care including the multiple options available for treatment of difficult fracture patterns or combinations of fractures about the knee. Case examples are provided to present treatment principles and lessons learned that can be applied to civilian fracture care about the knee. Copyright © 2010 by Lippincott Williams & Wilkins.
