TI  - Treatment of rectal war wounds
AU  - van Waes, O.J.F.
AU  - Halm, J.A.
AU  - Vermeulen, J.
AU  - McAlister, V.C.
PY  - 2014
PD  - 
N2  - Treatment strategies for penetrating rectal injuries (PRI) in civilian settings are still not uniformly agreed, in part since high-energy transfer PRI, such as is frequently seen in military settings, are not taken into account. Here, we describe three cases of PRI, treated in a deployed combat environment, and outline the management strategies successfully employed. We also discuss the literature regarding PRI management. Where there is a major soft tissue component, repetitive debridement and vacuum therapy is useful. A loop or end colostomy should be used, depending on the degree of damage to the anal sphincter complex.
