TI  - The father of pediatrical surgery and orthopedics as academical branches of science in Turkey: Ord. Prof. Dr. Aki̇f Şaki̇r Şakar (1888-1961)
AU  - Namal, A.
AU  - Aras, Ş.
AU  - Yürür, G.K.
PY  - 2008
PD  - 
N2  - Ord. Prof. Dr. Akif Şakir Şakar graduated from the Military School of Medicine in İstanbul in 1910. He was a student of the well-known physiologist Claude Bernard, and son of Şakir Paşa, the founder of physiology in Turkey. Starting with the first clinic he founded on 1929 within the structure of the İstanbul Medical School, he became a pioneer in the effort to establish a clinic of pediatrical surgery and orthopedics as a first of its kind in Turkey, as well as gaining a legitimization of this field as an area of specialization in Turkish medicine. In Turkey, pediatrical surgery and orthopedics could only gain the status of an area of specialization in 1947. Pediatrical surgery and orthopedics were seperated as areas of sub-speciality in 1972, to become seperate professions. In this article, we will introduce in detail the leading role of Ord. Prof. Akif Şakir Şakar in the history of pediatrical surgery and orthopedics in Turkey.
