TI  - War odontology
AU  - Bustillos, D.A.
PY  - 2009
PD  - 
N2  - We present two cases of patients with face bones comminuted fractures due to a bullet injury, treated with coadjuvant functional orthopaedic therapy (FOT). FOT helped to improve pain control, allowed harmonious growth and development of the involved areas and minimized the sequelae. Comminuted fractures of face bones produce very important sequelae, such as collapse and asymmetry of face areas. In conclusion: Coadjutant treatment with FOT in patients with posttraumatic bone and/or soft tissue loss in mouth, face, or neck prevents the dreaded sequelae, favours normal development and diminishes hospitalisation time. FOT reduces costs for National Health System and for the own patient in private medicine. FOT is a more cost-effective treatment for one of the consequences of the today's world violence.
