N2  - Louis Stromeyer was a pioneer of orthopaedic surgery and military medicine in Germany. The 200th anniversary of his birth was celebrated on 6 March 2004. He was much admired in Britain, which he visited on three occasions and where he met many of the country's leading surgeons. He was a friend and colleague of the London surgeon W J Little (1810–94), whose clubfoot he corrected by the operation he developed, and which Little introduced to Britain: subcutaneous tenotomy. A bibliography of Stromeyer's publications is appended. © 2006, Royal Society of Medicine Press Limited. All rights reserved.
